# Line endings: stored as LF in the repository, checked out in the platform's
# native style (CRLF on Windows). The factory reads both.
* text=auto
*.py   text
*.md   text
# CSV files are stored byte-for-byte: they use CRLF line endings by standard
# (RFC 4180), as written by Python's csv module and Excel. Converting them
# would make git report unchanged CSV files as modified.
*.csv  -text
*.json text
*.yml  text
